; ReviewCompiler[3]: `*` with no tracked score holders fails like NO_ENTITIES_FOUND (store success 0,
; `return run` fails) instead of succeeding with 0. A single-holder argument (`scoreboard players get`,
; `if score`) never resolves `*` (ScoreHolderArgument.getName passes an empty wildcard supplier).
; Results go to storage first: storing into a score would itself create a tracked holder.
@setup
objective create t dummy

@function wild_return
return run scoreboard players add * t 1

@function run
execute store success storage mcfc:wild set int 1 run scoreboard players set * t 1
execute store success storage mcfc:wild ret int 1 run function mcfc-test:wild_return
execute store success storage mcfc:wild reset int 1 run scoreboard players reset * t
scoreboard players set #h t 5
execute store success storage mcfc:wild get int 1 run scoreboard players get * t
data modify storage mcfc:wild if_ran set value 0
execute if score * t matches 5 run data modify storage mcfc:wild if_ran set value 1
execute store success storage mcfc:wild add int 1 run scoreboard players add * t 1
execute store result score set t run data get storage mcfc:wild set
execute store result score ret t run data get storage mcfc:wild ret
execute store result score reset t run data get storage mcfc:wild reset
execute store result score get t run data get storage mcfc:wild get
execute store result score add t run data get storage mcfc:wild add
execute store result score if_ran t run data get storage mcfc:wild if_ran

@validate
score set t is 0
score ret t is 0
score reset t is 0
score get t is 0
score if_ran t is 0
score add t is 1
score #h t is 6
